    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-79b54a27e35c\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"hook-no-nonzero-exit\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"process\\\\.exit\\\\(\\\\s*([1-9]|-)\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.ts\"},{\"id\":\"hook-no-nonzero-exitcode\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"process\\\\.exitCode\\\\s*=\\\\s*([1-9]|-)\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.ts\"},{\"id\":\"hook-no-plain-text-stdout\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"console\\\\.(log|info|debug)\\\\(\\\\s*[\\\"'\\\\x60][^{\\\\[]\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.ts\"}],\"coverage\":\"The flagrant literal violations in the added TypeScript lines of the hook files: `process.exit(...)` with a literal non-zero or negative code, `process.exitCode` set to a literal non-zero or negative value, and `console.log`, `console.info` or `console.debug` called with a string literal that does not start with `{` or `[`, which is plain non-JSON text on stdout.\",\"residual\":\"Does any path of the edited hook exit with a non-zero code (through a computed exit code, an uncaught exception or a rejected promise), run without its own timeout or time bound, or write anything to stdout other than the JSON the host expects?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/packages/hooks/src/guard.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export function fail(): never {\\n+  process.exit(1);\\n+}\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/packages/hooks/src/mark.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export function mark(): void {\\n+  process.exitCode = 2;\\n+}\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/packages/hooks/src/report.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export function report(): void {\\n+  console.log(\\\"hook finished\\\");\\n+}\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/packages/hooks/src/done.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\\n+export function done(out: object): never {\\n+  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(out));\\n+  process.exit(0);\\n+}\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"Literal non-zero exits and plain-text console output in the added hook code can be matched line by line. Other cases need judgement: computed exit codes, uncaught throws, whether the hook bounds its own time, and whether stdout writes are only the expected JSON. These depend on control flow and meaning, not literal text.\"}",
